Better long-term fix in your correlate app: Another item for Claude Code. The SVG lines probably use absolute stroke-width values. Add this to your prompt:
When generating SVGs for export, add vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" to line/path elements if you want strokes to stay consistent, OR (preferred for Inkscape compatibility) make sure all stroke-widths are set as proportional values and include the attribute style="vector-effect: none" on the root SVG so that Inkscape scales strokes with transforms. Also, avoid using SVG transform="scale()" on groups. Instead, set actual coordinate values so that when the user scales in Inkscape, everything behaves predictably.
The encoding issue you're seeing (the garbled text like "ÝÜOOîß" instead of gene names) is a separate problem. That's a character encoding mismatch in the SVG, likely UTF-8 vs Latin-1. Add this for Claude Code too:
Make sure the downloaded SVG file includes <?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?> at the top, and that the text content is properly encoded as UTF-8 when generating the SVG blob for download.
SVG export improvements for correlate.cmm.se
Fix these issues with the SVG download/export so that the files work properly in both Adobe Illustrator and Inkscape:

Encoding: Add <?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?> as the first line of the exported SVG. Make sure all text content is properly UTF-8 encoded in the SVG blob. Currently gene names display as garbled characters (mojibake) when opened in Illustrator.
SVG dimensions: Set explicit width and height attributes on the root <svg> element that match the viewBox (e.g., if viewBox is "0 0 800 600", set width="800" height="600"). Currently files open tiny in Inkscape.
Stroke scaling: Make sure stroke-widths on lines and edges use values that scale proportionally when the user resizes in Illustrator/Inkscape. Avoid using transform="scale()" on groups. Instead, compute actual coordinate values so scaling behaves predictably.
Optional: Add an "Export SVG (outlined text)" button that creates a second download option where all <text> elements are converted to <path> elements using opentype.js (CDN: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/opentype.js). This ensures fonts render correctly regardless of what's installed. Keep the normal SVG download with editable text as the default.

Apply these fixes to all SVG exports in the app (scatter plots, network graphs, box plots, etc.)


Fixes 1-3 are quick and will immediately make your life easier in both Illustrator and Inkscape. Fix 4 is the nice-to-have that solves the font reflow problem we hit earlier. You could do 1-3 first and add 4 later if needed.








